    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena saw a picture of the Great Bath at Mohenjo-daro.\n\"Cities were well planned,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "Harappa",
     "drain",
     "Dholavira"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Harappan cities such as Mohenjo-daro and Harappa had straight roads crossing at right angles, brick houses and covered drains. This shows careful town planning.\nWater was managed with wells, tanks and the Great Bath. Dholavira in Gujarat had a system of reservoirs to store rainwater.\nAround 1900 BCE the cities declined, perhaps due to climate change and drying rivers. People moved to new areas, so it was a change rather than a sudden end."
    }
   },
